//? Title: WaveNet stack:real audio and visible autoregressive fitting
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Genuine speaker-disjoint spoken-digit windows feed a complete gated causal stack. Explicit SGD references,all27 Adam updates,teacher-forced metrics and genuine sampled feedback reveal the limits of the short fit.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.9_1d_convolutions/wavenet_stack.cpp`.

> The method

Quantize original8kHz audio with tensor mu-law256,learn next-code distributions after127warmup samples,and expose every optimizer update. Restore76 learned arrays,verify causal prefixes,and generate256new codes per real prompt using only previous sampled codes.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/wavenet_stack_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/wavenet_stack_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/wavenet_stack_concept.tikz > build/wavenet_stack_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/wavenet_stack_concept.svg build/wavenet_stack_concept.dvi > build/wavenet_stack_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
