> Verification and limits

Native checks independently verify all33tiny parameter coordinates,causal
RF/future Jacobians,all76full-graph gradients,codec bins/stable masked loss
and every original27clip PCM/code/window/prompt sample. Every count and all
reference scores/metrics agree with retained host oracles. Public examples
compile/run;original three-epoch workflow and sampled generation pass.
The selected epoch1 has held-out NLL5.535256,compared with unigram4.940436
and transition4.603732. Its expected-amplitude MSE.000148357 also exceeds
transition.000114889 and persistence.000038697. Sampled waveforms reach
near unit amplitude despite the much quieter original seed;lower fitting NLL
does not establish a useful speech model. Independent NumPy/PCM checks match
all55296input/target values,1152prompt values,768inverse-CDF samples and
768seeded uniforms. A fresh-store replay matches all196608generation logits
from their actual preceding128seed/sampled codes exactly. Held-out
likelihoods,amplitude errors and sampled waveforms must be considered together.

> Conclusion

Original data and visible optimization establish a reproducible causal-audio example. Teacher-forced likelihood and sampled continuations measure different behavior;the tiny custom split and48ms rollouts support no intelligible-speech quality claim.

> References

- [van den Oord et al.(2016),WaveNet:A Generative Model for Raw Audio](https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.03499).
